15850 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Bitcoin is a decentralized electronic cash system where transactions occur without a central authority\056 Even though there is no single entity\024like a bank or a registry\024to verify identities and manage the ledger\054 the network enforces that specific Unspent Transaction Outputs \050UTXOs\0511\051 only move when valid conditions are met\056 Here\054 \042valid\042 does not mean the owner\047s identity has been verified\073 rather\054 it means cryptographic proof has been provided showing control over the private key capable of unlocking the asset\047s locking condition\056\n\nBitcoin\047s security relies on two mathematical structures\056 The first is Elliptic Curve Cryptography \050ECC\051\054 which protects the control over assets\024effectively the economic authority corresponding to ownership\024through a system where digital signatures generated by private keys are verified by public keys\056 The second is the SHA\055256 hash function\054 which is used in mining and linking blocks together\054 thereby supporting the cost structure of consensus and the integrity of the records\056 Combining these two pillars\054 Bitcoin simultaneously achieves proof of ownership without banks and a virtually immutable record\056)
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 15851 0 R
     /Pg 1688 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
