15863 0 obj
  << /ActualText (alone is not enough to unlock it\056\n\nTo transfer bitcoin\054 one must generate a digital signature using the private key\056 A digital signature is a piece of data that mathematically proves the \042authority to satisfy the locking condition\042\024in other words\054 the fact that \042I control the private key and I authorize this transaction\042\056 Network participants use the public key to verify that the signature is correct\056 This mechanism works because there is an asymmetry between the private key and the public key\056 Calculating a public key from a private key is simple\054 but reverse\055engineering a private key from a public key is practically impossible with current computers\056 This very asymmetry is the core premise underpinning the security of Bitcoin\047s digital signatures\0565\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
