15897 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The second pillar of Bitcoin\047s security is the SHA\055256 hash function\056 A hash function is a one\055way function that takes an input of arbitrary length and outputs a hash value of fixed length\056 The same input will always produce the same output\054 but even the slightest change in the input generates a completely different hash value\056 For instance\054 \042Hello\042 and \042Hello\056\042 differ by only a single        \176)
