15936 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The two mathematical pillars of Bitcoin discussed earlier rely on the premise that it is practically impossible to reverse\055engineer a private key from a public key\054 or to accelerate hash searches enough to neutralize the cost structure of Proof of Work\056 However\054 quantum computing2\051 research\054 which emerged in the 1980s\054 revealed the potential to fundamentally shake this premise with the introduction of Shor\047s Algorithm in the mid\0551990s\0567\056 As it became clear that quantum computers could solve specific mathematical problems at speeds incomparable to classical computers\054 the entirety of modern cryptography\054 including Bitcoin\054 was placed in a new threat environment\056)
     /K [ 6 ]
