  << /ActualText (The prospect that quantum computers could pose a long\055term threat to Bitcoin\047s cryptographic system is no longer confined to the realm of science fiction\056 In recent years\054 major technology companies have successively announced achievements demonstrating the scale and error\055correction potential of quantum computers\056 In 2023\054 IBM unveiled Condor\054 a 1\054121\055qubit quantum processor\054 breaking the 1\054000\055qubit barrier\05610\056 Subsequently\054 in its updated 2025 roadmap\054 IBM set a goal to develop the Starling system by 2029\054 which aims to perform 100 million quantum gate operations using 200 logical qubits\05611\056 Google announced Willow\054 a quantum chip equipped with 105 qubits\054 in December 2024\05612\056 Microsoft also announced the Majorana 1 chip in February 2025\054 stating it had laid the groundwork for scaling up to 1 million qubits on a single chip in the long term\05613\056)
