16099 0 obj
  << /ActualText (RSA is a widely used public\055key cryptosystem proposed in 1977 by Ronald Rivest\054 Adi Shamir\054 and Leonard Adleman\056 Its security is based on the computational difficulty of factoring a large composite number n\024formed by multiplying two large prime numbers\054 p and q\024back into its original prime factors\056 However\054 a sufficiently large fault\055tolerant quantum computer could solve this problem efficiently using Shor\047s Algorithm\056 Although RSA is not the digital signature scheme used by Bitcoin\054 it is frequently cited as a representative example when discussing the cryptographic threats posed by quantum computing\056)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 16100 0 R
     /Pg 5430 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
