16114 0 obj
  << /ActualText (An important point must be made here\072 the cryptographic threat posed by quantum computers is not confined to cryptocurrency\056 Bitcoin utilizes the secp256k1\055based elliptic curve signature scheme and the SHA\055256 hash function\054 but these are not isolated technologies created specifically for Bitcoin\056 More accurately\054 Bitcoin is built upon the core technological lineages of modern digital security infrastructure\072 public\055key cryptography\054 digital signatures\054 and cryptographic hash functions\056\n\nSHA\055256 is a representative cryptographic hash function belonging to the SHA\0552 family\054 an algorithm designed by the National Security Agency \050NSA\051 and published as a standard by the National Institute of Standards and Technology \050NIST\051\056 Today\054 SHA\0552 family hash functions are used in diverse areas such as digital signatures\054 certificates\054 software integrity verification\054 and secure communications\054 serving as a cryptographic foundation for data protection in online payments and cloud services\056 Transport Layer Security \050TLS\051\054 the core protocol for modern internet security\054 also operates on top of these cryptographic technologies\056 TLS is the standard protocol for encrypting internet communications and forms the security foundation for HTTPS traffic\056 When a user accesses a website starting with HTTPS in their browser\054 TLS verifies the server\047s identity through its certificate and agrees on a session key for secure communication\056 This process utilizes public\055key cryptography\054 digital signatures\054 certificates\054 and hash functions in tandem\073 furthermore\054 TLS is not a technology used solely for website access\056 The entire internet infrastructure\024including email security\054 cloud services\054 Application Programming Interface \050API\051 communications\054 and corporate networks\024relies on TLS and its surrounding authentication frameworks\056\n\n)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 16115 0 R
     /Pg 5708 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

