16123 0 obj
  << /ActualText (At the center of this process is the Public Key Infrastructure \050PKI\051\056 PKI is a system that uses digital certificates to guarantee that a specific public key actually belongs to a particular server or organization\056 Web browsers verify server certificates based on root certificates from trusted Certificate Authorities\054 thereby forming the chain of trust for internet communications\056 This structure has long relied on RSA or elliptic curve\055based public\055key cryptography and digital signatures\056 In other words\054 behind everyday actions like accessing websites\054 installing apps\054 receiving software updates\054 and storing data in the cloud\054 there is an invisible architecture of trust constructed by public\055key cryptography and hash functions\056\n\nThe traditional financial system is also not exempt from this structure\073 online banking authentication\054 the protection of financial transaction messages\054 card payment networks\054 international settlement systems\054 electronic document authentication\054 and software code signing all rely deeply on public\055key authentication\054 digital signatures\054 and encrypted communication technologies\056 The modern financial system operates atop a cryptographic trust architecture combining servers\054 certificates\054 keys\054 signatures\054 hashes\054 and security protocols\056 Therefore\054 if a sufficiently powerful quantum computer emerges\054 Bitcoin will not be the only entity affected\056 A vast array of fields that constitute digital trust\024including secure internet communications\054 digital signatures\054 certificates\054 financial transactions\054 software distribution\054 and government and public sector security systems\024would be simultaneously impacted\056 What is vulnerable to quantum computers is the entirety of modern civilization\047s digital security framework\054 and paradoxically\054 this very fact provides a degree of buffering for Bitcoin\056 This is because the Bitcoin community is not alone in needing to solve this problem\073 governments\054 enterprises\054 and research institutions worldwide are concurrently tackling the exact same issue\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 16124 0 R
     /Pg 6002 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

