16127 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This collective response is already underway\073 in August 2024\054 after an eight\055year international standardization process\054 NIST finalized and announced the first three Post\055Quantum Cryptography \050PQC\051 standards\05617\056\n\nThe first is ML\055KEM \050Module\055Lattice\055Based Key\055Encapsulation Mechanism\051\054 a key encapsulation method designed to allow communicating parties to securely share secret keys\054 intended to replace or supplement key exchange structures used in existing internet security protocols for a post\055quantum environment\056 The second is ML\055DSA \050Module\055Lattice\055Based Digital Signature Algorithm\051\054 a lattice\055based digital signature scheme aimed at replacing existing RSA or ECDSA signatures\056 The third is SLH\055DSA \050Stateless Hash\055Based Digital Signature Algorithm\051\054 a hash\055based digital signature scheme built on a different mathematical approach than ML\055DSA\054 proposed as a supplementary standard in case ML\055DSA proves vulnerable\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 16128 0 R
     /Pg 6002 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
