16219 0 obj
  << /ActualText (upgrade can still accept blocks generated under the new rules as valid\054 making it easier to preserve network backward compatibility\056 Conversely\054 a hardfork introduces an upgrade that is incompatible with legacy rules\056 In this scenario\054 if all participants do not upgrade simultaneously\054 the network faces the permanent risk of splitting into two independent blockchains operating under divergent rules\056 Historically\054 the Bitcoin ecosystem has prioritized network stability by leaning heavily toward the gradual\054 conservative nature of softforks\056\nA prime example of an upgrade successfully integrated into the mainnet through this rigorous process is Segregated Witness \050SegWit\051\054 activated in 2017\056 Introduced via a softfork\054 SegWit was defined in BIP\05514123\056 and separated signature \050witness\051 data from the core transaction structure\054 handling it in a distinct data architecture\056 In essence\054 it reorganized the transaction blueprint by decoupling the core transactional details from the cryptographic proofs verifying them\056\n\nSegWit also changed the calculation of block capacity from a strict byte limit to a weighted metric called \042Block Weight\054\042 under which witness data was discounted relative to base transaction data\056 This structural shift enhanced transaction flexibility and maximized block space efficiency\056 Ultimately\054 it achieved the dual benefit of maintaining flawless backward compatibility with the legacy network while effectively expanding the network\047s practical transaction throughput\05624\056\n\nThe activation of Taproot in 2021 marks another vital milestone in Bitcoin\047s evolution\056 Taproot introduced a highly flexible conditional spending framework and a new signature mechanism to the network\05625\056 Rather than entirely deprecating the legacy ECDSA signature scheme\054 it introduced the option to utilize Schnorr signatures within Taproot outputs and spending paths\056 Schnorr signatures provide the cryptographic foundation to aggregate multi\055signature transactions\054 making them appear as compact as single\055signature inputs\056\n\nFurthermore\054 Taproot was designed so that even if complex spending conditions are established\054 only the specific path executed during the transaction is exposed to the blockchain\056 For instance\054 if multiple unlocking conditions are predefined\054 any unused paths remain concealed\054 and only the active route is written on\055chain\056 Through this mechanism\054 Taproot significantly optimized data efficiency while vastly improving user privacy by preventing the exposure of unused spending conditions\056\n\nThe critical takeaway here is that Taproot did not abruptly disrupt Bitcoin\047s existing paradigm\056 It preserved legacy address types and signature methods while incrementally introducing new output types and spending mechanisms\056 Executed as a softfork\054 the upgrade successfully activated at Bitcoin mainnet block height 709\054632\056 Consequently\054 Taproot stands as a textbook example of how Bitcoin can safely accommodate innovative cryptographic signature schemes and complex conditional spending logic while maintaining its conservative consensus structure\056\n\nThe achievements of SegWit and Taproot demonstrate that Bitcoin is not a static\054 unchanging system\054 but a living system capable of deliberate\054 organic evolution\056 SegWit transformed the paradigm of transaction structures and block space utilization\054 while Taproot introduced next\055generation signature schemes and script expressions\056 Both major upgrades were achieved through prolonged verification and consensus within Bitcoin\047s inherently conservative     \176)
