  << /ActualText (factors\072 selecting appropriate quantum\055resistant signature algorithms and output structures\054 deploying them through a stable soft fork\054 securing support across wallets\054 exchanges\054 and infrastructure providers\054 and encouraging users to migrate their assets\056\n\nTechnical pathways can be designed\054 but they only become effective through voluntary adoption and decentralized coordination across the network\056 At this point\054 the discussion naturally turns to two additional challenges\072 the timeline of the transition itself and the question of how to deal with coins that do not\024or cannot\024participate in that transition\056 Depending on when a quantum threat emerges and how quickly the ecosystem responds\054 the process may unfold as an orderly technological evolution or as a race against time\056 The treatment of these non\055migrating coins therefore becomes one of the most important unresolved questions in Bitcoin\047s post\055quantum future\056)
