16298 0 obj
  << /ActualText (From the perspective of quantum vulnerability\054 not all Bitcoin Unspent Transaction Outputs \050UTXOs\051 share an identical risk profile\056 The critical determinant resides in whether a public key is already visibly exposed on the distributed ledger\054 and the duration for which that exposure has persisted\056 In the nascent stages of Bitcoin\054 the Pay\055to\055Public\055Key \050P2PK\051 script format was predominantly utilized\056 Under P2PK\054 the public key is directly embedded within the locking script \050scriptPubKey\051\056 Consequently\054 from the exact moment of output creation\054 the public key is exposed on the blockchain\056 Should future quantum computers achieve sufficient logical qubit capacity\054 these specific UTXOs will become the primary targets for long\055exposure attacks\054 as adversaries can attempt to derive the corresponding private keys directly from these visible public keys\056\n\nConversely\054 under the Pay\055to\055Public\055Key\055Hash \050P2PKH\051 framework\054 which has been widely adopted in subsequent years\054 it is not the raw public key but its cryptographic hash that is recorded on\055chain\056 Within this architecture\054 the public key remains completely concealed until the asset is actively spent\056 Because a public key hash represents an additional layer of cryptographic compression\054 it is computationally infeasible for an attacker to deduce the public key from the hash alone\056 In this regard\054 P2PKH exhibits a significantly lower vulnerability to long\055exposure quantum attacks compared to its predecessor\054 P2PK\056\n\nNevertheless\054 P2PKH does not afford absolute immunity against quantum threats\056 The vulnerability manifests the precise instant a UTXO is spent\054 as the transaction must expose the raw public key to the network for verification\056 Under ordinary circumstances\054 this brief exposure carries nominal risk\073 once the transaction is validated and finalized\054 the target UTXO is entirely consumed\056 If no residual balance remains at that address\054 an adversary deriving the private key gains nothing\056 However\054 the paradigm shifts                        \176)
     /K [ 6 ]
     /P 16299 0 R
     /Pg 8532 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

