16341 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This structural bifurcation becomes particularly relevant when analyzing Bitcoin\047s oldest\054 dormant allocations\056 During the network\047s infancy\054 P2PK outputs\024which directly expose the public key\024were standard\054 and a significant portion of these funds has remained entirely motionless to this day\056 Most notable among these are the approximately 1\0560 to 1\0561 million bitcoins29\056 estimated to have been mined by Satoshi Nakamoto\054 an allocation that serves as a recurring focal point in post\055quantum security discourse\056\n\nThe gravity of the Satoshi coins dilemma is self\055evident\056 Should a large amount of bitcoin associated with the creator suddenly move via quantum exploitation\054 the global market would unlikely perceive it as a localized security breach\056 Instead\054 it would be interpreted as a signal that Bitcoin\047s oldest cryptographic locks have been compromised\054 compounded by the sudden materialization of a large potential supply overhang\056 Representing roughly 5\045 of the total 21\055million hard\055capped supply\054 the mere perception that this supply has become liquid or vulnerable to market dumping could deliver a severe shock to Bitcoin\047s valuation and systemic credibility\056)
     /K [ 19 ]
     /P 16342 0 R
     /Pg 9202 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

