16358 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The governance choices available to the ecosystem can be categorized into four primary paradigms\056\n\nThe first paradigm is the Status Quo\056 Under this approach\054 ownership within Bitcoin is defined strictly by the ability to produce a valid signature\054 regardless of identity\054 intent\054 or how long the coins have been held\056 Even if a public key is exposed on\055chain and someone uses a quantum computer to compute the corresponding private key and produce a valid signature\054 the network does not block the transaction\056 Under this approach\054 a quantum\055driven transaction is not seen as an external attack\054 but rather as a natural consequence of the cryptographic foundation becoming no longer sufficiently difficult to break\056 The advantage is clear\072 the network does not judge ownership after the fact\054 does    \176)
