16457 0 obj
  << /ActualText (No confirmed case exists in which Bitcoin\047s core cryptographic mechanisms or consensus system has been compromised by an external attack\054 resulting in the theft of assets at the network level\056 However\054 critical vulnerabilities have been discovered in the code\056 In August 2010\054 a transaction exploiting an integer overflow bug was included in block 74\054638\054 creating approximately 184\0564 billion bitcoins\056 Developers quickly released a patched version\054 and the network abandoned the affected branch and reorganized onto the valid chain\056 In 2018\054 CVE\0552018\05517144 was disclosed\056 The vulnerability enabled denial\055of\055service \050DoS\051 attacks through duplicate\055input handling and\054 more seriously\054 could have allowed inflation of the bitcoin supply\056 Fortunately\054 a patched release was issued before the vulnerability could be exploited\056 Together\054 these incidents demonstrate not only that Bitcoin is not a flawless system\054 but also how an open\055source consensus protocol can identify vulnerabilities\054 address them\054 and continuously improve itself\056\n\042Bitcoin Block 74\054638\054\042 Blockchain\056com Explorer\054 mined August 15\054 2010\054 )
     /K [ 11 ]
     /P 16462 0 R
     /Pg 11868 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
